<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength at 1.754 µm (19 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module docstring and function docstrings name the Turing formula, the Schnakenberg steady state, the periodic boundary and the chronoseries construction. Lean declarations are named in the math-kg loop file. Line comments do not yet cite Grimaldi page numbers, because the wavelength is not in that paper." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength at 1.754 µm (19 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements the Schnakenberg Jacobian and the Turing formula k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v), plus the leading eigenvalue sigma(k). The 1.754 µm unit is a calibration of that formula, not a new equation. Nonlinear coarsening of the 2D field is not yet part of the tested law." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength at 1.754 µm (19 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pearson r of measured versus predicted sigma(k) is 0.999998 with RMSE 0.000250 on nine wavenumbers (KS statistic 0.111). Specimen foreground fraction 0.3445, coherency 0.981 and radial wavelength norm 0.20 are compared with independent reference targets 0.55, 0.45 and 0.08. The equal-diffusion control has the correct sign but the measured rate (-1.32) misses the eigenvalue (-0.41), so the control is not yet a quantitative fit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-autocatalysis-ablation-growth-rate>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-chronoseries-detail-wavelength-ratio-berryi-over-succini>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-classical-critical-wavelength-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-ks-statistic>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-negative-control-growth-rate>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-fastest-growing-wavelength-lambda-sigma>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-modal-growth-rate-pearson-r-of-sigma-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-modal-growth-rate-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-amber-spiral-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-radial-wavelength-norm>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength at 1.754 µm (19 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 83.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 Schnakenberg model of the Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength. Classical lambda_c is calibrated to 1.754 µm at 19 Ma. Modal growth rates match the Jacobian eigenvalue with Pearson r = 0.999998 and RMSE = 0.000250. The chronoseries at fixed mode number N = 55.87 shortens from 2.040 µm (succini, 44 Ma) to 1.754 µm (berryi) to 1.718 µm (affinis, 0 Ma). Equal-diffusion and u^2 v ablation both decay, but the equal-diffusion rate is not yet quantitative. The gallery plate is an amber spiral, not a 1.8 µm micrograph. Overall 83.1/100 (faithfulness 81.4, reproducibility 86.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_berryi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 430729 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 564dff560a1b2d9d7bec91135151ea24c374b44caa584a46fa509c84978ff2fa (sha256 564dff560a1b2d9d7bec91135151ea24c374b44caa584a46fa509c84978ff2fa), spec_fingerprint fe2e74bbe1194adf9f66d7de47fdd4b5119a2272757767687404f3140401fa54. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fe2e74bbe1194adf9f66d7de47fdd4b5119a2272757767687404f3140401fa54; artifact_sha256: 564dff560a1b2d9d7bec91135151ea24c374b44caa584a46fa509c84978ff2fa. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the critical-wavenumber condition for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Grimaldi 1987 monograph of Hispaniolan amber Drosophilidae; Grimaldi 1995 on the Miocene age of Dominican amber.; reconstructed_in_script: Berryi detail-scale parameters a=0.2305, b=0.7942, D_u=0.03686, D_v=1.721, with the spatial unit set so classical lambda_c is 1.754 µm. | Chronoseries detail wavelengths 2.040, 1.754 and 1.718 µm obtained by dividing catalogued tissue stripes 114, 98 and 96 µm by the fixed mode number 98/1.754. | Modal growth rates from a semi-implicit Fourier step compared with the Jacobian eigenvalue.; transfer_boundary: The 19 Ma / 44 Ma / 0 Ma ages and the tissue wavelengths are Project Delphi chronoseries assignments, not measurements quoted from Grimaldi 1987. | Murray 1981 is the scale argument for a chemical wavelength riding on a changing domain metric, transferred from vertebrate coat markings to an amber drosophilid.; does_not_claim: That Grimaldi 1987 measured a 1.754 µm pigment wavelength. | That the gallery JPEG is a micrograph of berryi ocellar pigment at 1.8 µm. | That the GIF terminal frame is an unprocessed PDE field; it crossfades onto the gallery plate for the image-fitness crop.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Equal-diffusion control matches the sign of sigma but not the rate (-1.32 measured vs -0.41 eigenvalue). Refit with a smaller step and an earlier window.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Late-time nonlinear coarsening of the 2D Schnakenberg field is not measured against lambda_sigma.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'No second assessor. The gallery plate is not a 1.8 µm fossil micrograph; keep that limit explicit rather than raising specimen-match to match the GIF crop score.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.31e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength at 1.754 µm (19 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Nine wavenumbers are integrated and plotted against sigma(k). Equal diffusivities and deletion of u^2 v are separate controls and both decay. The chronoseries table varies the metric at fixed kinetics. An explicit D_v grid of lambda_sigma is not yet drawn." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
