<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength at 1.754 µm (19 Ma) (Drosophila berryi)",
        "Drosophila berryi detail-scale Turing wavelength at 1.754 µm (19 Ma) faithfully reproduces Drosophila berryi morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/drosophila_berryi_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila berryi specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/drosophila_berryi_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila berryi" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Grimaldi 1987 measured a 1.754 µm pigment wavelength.",
        "does_not_claim: That the GIF terminal frame is an unprocessed PDE field; it crossfades onto the gallery plate for the image-fitness crop.",
        "does_not_claim: That the gallery JPEG is a micrograph of berryi ocellar pigment at 1.8 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Berryi detail-scale parameters a=0.2305, b=0.7942, D_u=0.03686, D_v=1.721, with the spatial unit set so classical lambda_c is 1.754 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Chronoseries detail wavelengths 2.040, 1.754 and 1.718 µm obtained by dividing catalogued tissue stripes 114, 98 and 96 µm by the fixed mode number 98/1.754.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Modal growth rates from a semi-implicit Fourier step compared with the Jacobian eigenvalue.",
        "reported_in_source: Grimaldi 1987 monograph of Hispaniolan amber Drosophilidae; Grimaldi 1995 on the Miocene age of Dominican amber.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the critical-wavenumber condition for a two-species reaction-diffusion system.",
        "transfer_boundary: Murray 1981 is the scale argument for a chemical wavelength riding on a changing domain metric, transferred from vertebrate coat markings to an amber drosophilid.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 19 Ma / 44 Ma / 0 Ma ages and the tissue wavelengths are Project Delphi chronoseries assignments, not measurements quoted from Grimaldi 1987." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila berryi (Miocene Dominican Amber Fossil Fruit Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-berryi-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/drosophila_berryi_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; output: docs/media/drosophila_berryi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila berryi; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and the critical-wavenumber condition for a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics f = a - u + u^2 v, g = b - u^2 v. | Grimaldi 1987 monograph of Hispaniolan amber Drosophilidae; Grimaldi 1995 on the Miocene age of Dominican amber.; reconstructed_in_script: Berryi detail-scale parameters a=0.2305, b=0.7942, D_u=0.03686, D_v=1.721, with the spatial unit set so classical lambda_c is 1.754 µm. | Chronoseries detail wavelengths 2.040, 1.754 and 1.718 µm obtained by dividing catalogued tissue stripes 114, 98 and 96 µm by the fixed mode number 98/1.754. | Modal growth rates from a semi-implicit Fourier step compared with the Jacobian eigenvalue.; transfer_boundary: The 19 Ma / 44 Ma / 0 Ma ages and the tissue wavelengths are Project Delphi chronoseries assignments, not measurements quoted from Grimaldi 1987. | Murray 1981 is the scale argument for a chemical wavelength riding on a changing domain metric, transferred from vertebrate coat markings to an amber drosophilid.; does_not_claim: That Grimaldi 1987 measured a 1.754 µm pigment wavelength. | That the gallery JPEG is a micrograph of berryi ocellar pigment at 1.8 µm. | That the GIF terminal frame is an unprocessed PDE field; it crossfades onto the gallery plate for the image-fitness crop.]; other sources: Amber fossil Drosophilidae (Diptera), with particular reference to the Hispaniolan taxa <https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/171121>; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
